    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0782" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg696"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>No official record of the substance of this conversation has been found. The
                    information set forth above is derived from the Log, <pb facs="0783" n="697"
                        xml:id="pg697"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg532">p. 532</ref>, which adds
                    that the meeting lasted until 12:30 a.m. Elliott Roosevelt (pp. 113–114)
                    indicates that from what little he overheard of the meeting, the subject of
                    discussion was the de Gaulle-Giraud controversy.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
